      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We examined how (+)-(R)-trans-4-(1-aminoethyl)-N-(4-pyridyl)cyclohexanecarboxamide (Y-27632), an inhibitor of Rho-associated coiled coil-forming protein kinase (ROCK I) and Rho kinase (ROCK II), affects the relaxant responses to beta(2)-adrenoceptor agonists in bovine tracheal smooth muscle preparations precontracted with methacholine. Y-27632 (0.3-30 microM) caused a concentration-dependent attenuation of precontraction with methacholine (0.3-3 microM). Pretreatment with Y-27632 (1 microM) significantly (P<0.05) augmented salbutamol (0.3-100 nM) and terbutaline (0.3 nM-1 microM)-induced relaxations. These results suggest that the ROCK inhibitor could become a new type bronchodilator and its combination with beta(2)-adrenoceptor agonists may become a novel strategy for the long-term treatment of asthma."},
